From 2caeaf98f22079f98c8c0f8850aa83cc5eea68a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fruscai <103607006+fruscai@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 18:34:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Add "Save with embedded samples" save option

Writes each referenced sample into the project file as base64 instead of
pointing at it on disk, so the project opens and plays on a machine that
does not have the audio files. This is the same idea as a project bundle,
minus the folder: the result is still a single .mmpz.

The save path already threaded a bool down to DataFile::writeFile for
bundling. There are three ways to save now, so that becomes a SaveMode
enum and embedResources() sits next to copyResources(), walking the same
ELEMENTS_WITH_RESOURCES map.

Two things worth calling out:

Embedded audio carries no sample rate. SampleBuffer::fromBase64 assumes
the engine rate while fromFile hands back the file's own rate, so a
sample recorded at anything else plays back at the wrong speed. A 48 kHz
source embedded as-is renders a 220 Hz tone at 202 Hz. embedResources()
converts to the engine rate through AudioResampler first.

AudioResampler always passes end_of_input = 0, so libsamplerate keeps the
last frames in its filter delay and never flushes them, truncating the
end of every sample (144 frames for a 48 kHz source at SincBest). The
input is padded with silence to push the tail through and the output is
cut back to the expected length.

"src" is read before "sampledata" when loading, so it is removed rather
than blanked. factorysample: references are left alone, since they
resolve on any install and embedding them only inflates the file.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
